  "description_html": "Known distribution of mosasaur <i>Prognathodon</i>, based on fossil sites, added onto a map of the Late Cretaceous. Follows <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Takuya_Konishi/publication/237169671_The_northernmost_occurrence_of_Prognathodon_Squamata_Mosasauridae_from_the_Western_Interior_Seaway_of_North_America/links/00b7d5290181e4746b000000/The-northernmost-occurrence-of-Prognathodon-Squamata-Mosasauridae-from-the-Western-Interior-Seaway-of-North-America.pdf\">Konishi (2012)</a> (p. 1113), but with tooth icons replaced with larger dots for clarity. The map also contains sites with fossils attributed to <i>Dollosaurus</i>, synonymized with <i>Prognathodon</i>, following <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/235806607_On_the_occurrence_of_a_giant_flying_reptile_Pterosauria_in_the_terminal_Late_Cretaceous_of_the_Lower_Volga_Region\">Averaniov &amp; Yarkov (2004)</a> and <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/237212182_Dental_and_vertebral_morphology_of_the_enigmatic_mosasaur_Dollosaurus_Reptilia_Mosasauridae_from_the_lower_Campanian_Upper_Cretaceous_of_southern_Sweden\">Lindgren (2005)</a>. Base map based on <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LateCretaceousMap.jpg\" title=\"File:LateCretaceousMap.jpg\">figure from Mannion, P. D. (2013)</a>.",
